{
  "text": "Our heart is a muscular organ which is protected by the rib cage. The heart is divided into four chambers. The two upper chambers of heart are called right a trim and left a trim. And the two lower chambers of heart are called right ventricle and left ventricle. In-period venaciva and superior venaciva carry the oxygenated blood to the right aitrium of the heart. Blood flows from the right aitrium into the right ventricle through the open tricuspid wall. When the ventricles are full the tricuspid wall shuts. Blood leads the right ventricle through the pulmonary wall into the pulmonary aitry for oxygenation. The pulmonary veins carry oxygenated blood to the left aitrium. Blood flows from the left aitrium into the left ventricle through the open metal wall. When the ventricles are full the metal wall shuts. Blood leaves the left ventricle through the aitric wall into the aitre and to the body. And this is how the heart functions continuously.",
